{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-19T06:00:07.038Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.2-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"4d9762431f0373f5e006e213","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.2-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-19T06:00:07.038Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-19T06:00:07.036Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Gaps ranked by expected recurring output savings under pm core 2026.11.18: (1) task-ranked recall avoids a 134-token projected item read plus triage of generic recall for a known task; (2) freshness and contradiction checks avoid rereading competing sources, with value on loops that encounter divergent facts; (3) federation avoids repeated repository lookups on cross-project loops. Consolidation already offers review and apply, so it ranks below these gaps. Public main baseline on pm-memory-higm: orientation 692 tokens, orientation with a 700-token ceiling 552, brief get 390 and projected get 134, using ceiling UTF-8 bytes divided by four. Implement task-ranked recall as a read-only SDK projection."}]}],"before_hash":"0784e9ff3b284e64ac79b4fcb43495aa153a24ac0ea60e11898ed3c56301a9cd","after_hash":"d147454fe5a9d8136c6abcb1ba29e3d6c64b30c967551f1f531bda6a69cab0c5","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"76615a7e1017f982ed240660f5f1dee4d890f8d39c376ee33fb1c2a100e575c6"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-19T06:02:06.483Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.2-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"4d9762431f0373f5e006e213","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.2-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-19T06:02:06.483Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Design: take a native item ID, read one certified SDK corpus, prefer explicitly linked eligible Knowledge, and fall back to task-title and description lexical matches when there are no eligible links. Exclude consent-managed, archived, stale and noncurrent guidance using existing metadata. The resume intent uses rank-order whole-row admission and the SDK output fit and omission receipts. Reads leave the exposure ledger unchanged and do not use embeddings."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-19T06:02:06.483Z"}],"before_hash":"d147454fe5a9d8136c6abcb1ba29e3d6c64b30c967551f1f531bda6a69cab0c5","after_hash":"f68f58ab8d5865df0c71615685538cc657ca12ff6a0da7895b8471c81183a87c","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"53dfd8dfaa5add034c500db028f83c815681a997f4574eac0f4b9cea2d56beef"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-19T06:08:35.666Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.2-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"4d9762431f0373f5e006e213","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.2-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-19T06:08:35.666Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Public scratch tracker measurement, core 2026.11.18 at public commit 962af3e: both paths return the same two complete CI facts. Projected item read 134 plus generic recall 276 gives 410 TOON tokens versus 115, saving 295 (72%). Title-only read plus recall gives 307 versus 115, saving 192 (63%). JSON 615 versus 182 saves 433 (70%). Two public facts and four synthetic distractors were seeded only in the scratch copy. A second projected source read was 105 tokens (pm-memory-smuq), a gross cost proxy for freshness diagnostics. Another bounded orientation was 552 tokens on the same tracker layout, a gross cost proxy for cross-project loops. Those gaps are tracked by pm-memory-recall-freshness and pm-memory-recall-federation."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-19T06:08:35.666Z"}],"before_hash":"f68f58ab8d5865df0c71615685538cc657ca12ff6a0da7895b8471c81183a87c","after_hash":"b6d4720f166f4ae2260425c5e3b2b557c84c5b49982ff41deaa7009a513a9a63","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c9e553b5861bbfdadb1f2e4806b7dbe27851b125084cbfa1b43908051b6af173"}
